{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1344751-necromancy-in-3rd-edition-the-prince-resplendant-in-the-ruin-of-ages","id":1344751,"title":"Necromancy in 3rd edition (The Prince Resplendant in the Ruin of Ages)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-30T14:36:55-07:00","id":1344751,"title":"Necromancy in 3rd edition (The Prince Resplendant in the Ruin of Ages)","content":"We've got our first Abyssal NPC since the core book (whose Abyssal entry was 95% the same as a Solar) out today.<br /> <br /> Most of his charms are still pretty much the same as Solar ones, as they're covering basic techniques; seeing and attacking ghosts, leaping a range band, ignoring overwhelming penalties to his Parry, etc. The only new charm (which I think is quite fun) is a Craft charm for making traps out of corpses.<br /> <br /> But what's really interesting is that he's got Necromancy: a ritual (get sorcerous motes when you start the scene in a place of death), and 3 necromancy spells. The spells aren't obscure ideas either, they're straight-up the sort of thing I want to see necromancers doing: talking/seeing through a skull (it's a well-designed spell; there are now 3 or 4 communication spells, but they all have different advantages and disadvantages), animating a unit of zombies that last until they're under a full scene of sunlight (which means you could animate them in a daytime battle, and they wouldn't collapse until the end of the scene), and summoning a Mortwright or other monstrous ghost.<br /> <br /> I'm extremely curious as to whether the Prince can animate a Size 2 unit of zombies because he's Essence 2, and whether an Essence 5 necromancer could animate a Size 5 unit of zombies. Of course, you'd need to have access to a thousand corpses, so...<br /> <br /> It's just an Antagonists of the Righteous pdf, not the final Abyssal book, so I wouldn't be surprised if there's small tweaks to the ritual and these spells, but it's a good start, and gives us some rules for some low-level necromancy, which is nice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T20:36:28-07:00","id":1344821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1344751-necromancy-in-3rd-edition-the-prince-resplendant-in-the-ruin-of-ages#post1344751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm extremely curious as to whether the Prince can animate a Size 2 unit of zombies because he's Essence 2, and whether an Essence 5 necromancer could animate a Size 5 unit of zombies. Of course, <b>you'd need to have access to a thousand corpses, so...</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a house that can do that in one go. Ask for Rob.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name"